        "text": "The break statement\nLet\u2019s play with the trusty while loop. Type this:\n$number = 0\nwhile ( $number -ne 5) { $number ++\nif ($number -eq 3) {\nbreak\n}\nWrite-Host \"The number is $number\"\n}\nHopefully, you\u2019ll see that the last number printed is 2 . The conditional if statement says to stop\nlooping if $number is 3 . The break statement only acts on the loop it is nested inside.",
